d falling sounds for her  character along with the dialogue  coraline  coraline jones  leica's 2012 stop-motion movie film  paranorman has quite the cast of quirky  yet lovable characters including pitch  perfect star anna kendrick who voices  courtney the older sister of the title  character paranorman was kendrick's  first animated film as it debuted four  years before the release of trolls where  she voiced the lovable poppy in  paranorman kendrick was able to channel  her inner teenage girl from crushing on  boys talking on the phone and being  annoyed by her little brother the film's  directors chris butler and sam fell even  encouraged kendrick to do a surprising  amount of improv and ad living what are  you gonna do ask the zombies not to eat  you johnny depp and tim burton were  making movies together left and right  when he was chosen to voice victor in  burton's stop-motion film corpse bride  despite being one of the biggest stars  in the industry at the time corpse bride  just so happened to be depp's first  voice acting role in a film having only  previously done voice work as a guest  for an episode of king of the hill a  year prior one of the biggest challenges  of doing voice work for corpse bride was  that depp wasn't able to put together  his own character like he had done for  jack sparrow despite that depp was still  able to put his own spin on victor  where is your chakra  pixar's oscar-winning coco features an  all latino voice cast in order to stay  true to the story's ties to the mexican  holiday dia de los muertos gael garcia  bernal known for his roles in old and  mozart in the jungle jumped at the  opportunity to voice hector as he saw  that the role would give him the  opportunity to be part of something that  his children could watch and enjoy  bernal had always been a fan of pixar  and was truly drawn to the project  because of the world the film builds and  the cultural elements  you're always this nervous before a  performance much of 